  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved Labour market and employment policies and support to MSMEs in Fiji</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ILO is helping Fiji develop its National Employment Policy (NEP), a comprehensive framework promoting full employment and decent work for all, aligned with the SDGs. The NEP integrates employment into national policy, aiming for a dynamic and inclusive labour market through job creation, skills development, and equal opportunity.
The NEP draft was finalized through broad consultations with government agencies, employers, workers, and other stakeholders. The government plans to adopt the NEP in mid-2025, followed by implementation based on its action plan. This work is supported by the ILO-led joint programme &quot;Advancing the SDGs by improving livelihoods and resilience via economic diversification and digital transformation&quot;, funded by the Joint SDG Fund.
A key part of this initiative is improving labour statistics. The ILO has provided training and support to the National Statistics Office (NSO) and labour ministries to enhance their capacity to collect and analyze labour market data. In 2024, the ILO supported a Labour Force Survey, with results expected to be published by the NSO in mid-2025.</narrative>
  </description>
